Register the goodix5120 driver in a libfprint tree.

Apply from the libfprint source root after copying this directory's
goodix5120*.c / goodix5120*.h to libfprint/drivers/goodix5120/:

    patch -p1 < libfprint-register.patch

The driver is marked optional, so it is only built when named explicitly
(-Ddrivers=...,goodix5120). 27c6:5120 deliberately stays in libfprint's
"known unsupported" allowlist (libfprint/fprint-list-udev-hwdb.c and
data/autosuspend.hwdb) until the driver is part of the default set; the
hwdb tool prints a warning about the overlap, which is expected.

Written against libfprint master 6f9479c ("synaptics: Add new PID 0x10b").

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -141,6 +141,9 @@
     'upeksonly': {},
     'upekts': {},
     'goodixmoc': {},
+    # Goodix 27c6:5120 behind an ITE EC (Huawei MateBook). Optional: it needs
+    # the device's TLS PSK from a file and has not been run on hardware yet.
+    'goodix5120': { 'helper': ['openssl', 'pixman'], 'optional': true },
     'nb1010': {},
     'fpcmoc': {},
     'realtek': {},
--- a/libfprint/meson.build
+++ b/libfprint/meson.build
@@ -134,6 +134,11 @@
         'drivers/goodixmoc/goodix.c',
         'drivers/goodixmoc/goodix_proto.c',
     ),
+    'goodix5120' : files(
+        'drivers/goodix5120/goodix5120.c',
+        'drivers/goodix5120/goodix5120_proto.c',
+        'drivers/goodix5120/goodix5120_tls.c',
+    ),
     'fpcmoc' : files('drivers/fpcmoc/fpc.c'),
     'realtek' : files('drivers/realtek/realtek.c'),
     'focaltech_moc' : files('drivers/focaltech_moc/focaltech_moc.c'),
